questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a Spring Boot microservice periodically crashes with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space`. Profiling indicates that the Old Generation retains gigabytes of large byte payloads. You identify the following service component:

java
@Service
public class OrderProcessingService {
    private static final ThreadLocal<Map<String, Object>> AUDIT_CONTEXT = new ThreadLocal<>();

    @Async("fixedThreadPoolTaskExecutor")
    @Transactional
    public CompletableFuture<Void> processOrder(Order order) {
        Map<String, Object> ctx = Optional.ofNullable(AUDIT_CONTEXT.get()).orElseGet(HashMap::new);
        ctx.put("orderId", order.getId());
        ctx.put("payload", order.getRawBinaryPayload()); // ~10MB per order
        AUDIT_CONTEXT.set(ctx);

        persistOrder(order);
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(null);
    }
}
